---
import BaseLayout from "../../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetaPill from "../../../components/ui/MetaPill.astro";
import registry from "../../../data/phase-90-markets-firms-competition-corporate-power-democratic-economic-governance-registry.json";

const firms = registry.firm_formation_ownership_control_governance_dossiers;
const markets = registry.market_structure_competition_pricing_conduct_ledgers;
const power = registry.corporate_power_platform_supply_chain_public_support_registers;
const governance = registry.democratic_economic_governance_rights_remedy_long_horizon_ledgers;
---

<BaseLayout title="Markets, Firms, Competition, Corporate Power And Democratic Economic Governance | FTFN" description="Thirty-two inactive firm, market, competition, corporate-power, public-support, rights, remedy, and democratic-governance records.">
  <section class="page-section hero" data-markets-firms-economic-governance-registry><div class="hero__copy"><div class="eyebrow">FTFN / Economic Governance</div><h1 class="page-title">A firm count is not a competitive market, and corporate disclosure is not democratic accountability.</h1><p class="lede">Phase 90 traces who owns and controls firms; how actual markets, prices, quality, labor and innovation behave; how platform, supply-chain, financial, political and public-support power accumulates; and whether democratic institutions can protect rights, impose remedies and secure durable public value.</p><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label="8 inactive firm dossiers" tone="possibility" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive market ledgers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive power registers" /><MetaPill label="8 inactive governance ledgers" /><MetaPill label="0 market-governance decisions" tone="review" /></div></div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Firm Formation, Ownership, Control And Governance</div><h2>Eight firm dossiers remain closed.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/firm-formation-enterprise-lifecycle-001/">Read the enterprise-lifecycle guide</a></div><div class="grid">{firms.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.firm_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/markets-firms-economic-governance/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Entity identity, enterprise groups, beneficial ownership, control, boards, duties, capital, labor, public support, disclosure, restructuring, closure, succession, distribution, review, and receipts remain empty.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Market Structure, Competition, Pricing And Conduct</div><h2>Eight market ledgers contain no competition finding.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/market-structure-concentration-entry-contestability-001/">Read the market-structure guide</a></div><div class="grid">{markets.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><div class="meta-row"><MetaPill label={record.market_state} tone="review" /><MetaPill label="20 inactive gates" /></div><h3><a href={'/evidence/markets-firms-economic-governance/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.market_structure_competition_pricing_conduct_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Market boundaries, participants, shares, entry, switching, concentration, power, prices, quality, labor, suppliers, conduct, innovation, mergers, remedies, and distribution remain unassessed.</p></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Corporate, Platform, Supply-Chain And Public-Support Power</div><h2>Eight corporate-power registers remain inactive.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/platforms-data-algorithms-network-effects-001/">Read the platform-power guide</a></div><div class="source-list">{power.map((record) => <article class="source-row"><div><h3><a href={'/evidence/markets-firms-economic-governance/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.corporate_power_platform_supply_chain_public_support_register_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Ownership networks, creditors, platforms, data, algorithms, supply chains, financialization, lobbying, subsidies, tax expenditures, procurement, public returns, accountability, and crisis risk remain unassessed.</p></div><MetaPill label={record.power_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Democratic Economic Governance, Rights, Remedies And Long-Horizon Market Health</div><h2>Eight governance ledgers contain no public-value finding.</h2></div><a class="inline-link" href="/briefings/corporate-support-accountability-rights-remedies-public-value-001/">Read the accountability guide</a></div><div class="grid">{governance.map((record) => <article class="record-card"><h3><a href={'/evidence/markets-firms-economic-governance/' + record.slug + '/'}>{record.democratic_economic_governance_rights_remedy_long_horizon_ledger_id}: {record.named_entity}</a></h3><p>Standing, participation, enforcement, structural and conduct remedies, restitution, merger review, enterprise plurality, worker and consumer rights, public returns, coordination, resilience, and audit remain inactive.</p><MetaPill label={record.governance_state} tone="review" /></article>)}</div></section>

  <section class="page-section briefing-band"><div class="briefing-band__copy"><div class="eyebrow">Public Contract</div><h2>Inspect the empty market-governance state.</h2><p>The export publishes the complete control surface without treating firm counts as competition, lower prices as complete welfare, concentration as proven abuse, profit as productive investment, merger approval as public benefit, or disclosure as democratic accountability—and without classifying, defining, finding, approving, subsidizing, remedying, scoring, ranking, or changing a stage.</p></div><article class="record-card"><a class="inline-link" href="/data/markets-firms-competition-corporate-power-democratic-economic-governance.json">Markets, firms, competition, and governance JSON</a></article></section>
</BaseLayout>
